  "origin": {
    "kind": "port",
    "repository": "kieranklaassen/kkfonie",
    "commit": "808719d0190315e5c6991833fe4e51c24ae75d3f",
    "files": [
      {
        "path": "Tatami/Source/Devices/Instruments/EmberParams.h",
        "sha256": "4a2cf92811e96c0a58e74144d0122b328e9dc031555f115b8316e69dad95b6e3",
        "portedTo": "cpp/devices/ember/device.json",
        "deviations": [
          "lfo1Sync, lfo1Division, lfo2Sync and lfo2Division are dropped: the device ABI has no tempo. Both LFOs always run at their rate in Hz. The other 43 parameters keep their ids, order, ranges and defaults.",
          "Labelled discrete parameters (oscillator and LFO shapes, osc2Sync, filterType, filterSlope, LFO destinations, voiceMode) are choice parameters. osc1Coarse, osc2Coarse and unisonVoices stay numeric and are rounded to whole numbers by the device.",
          "JUCE skew factors became tapers: cutoff (skew 0.25), the eight envelope times and both LFO rates (skew 0.3) are log; glide (skew 0.4, minimum 0) is linear.",
          "The '%' unit on 0..1 amounts is left out; the values are unchanged.",
          "kPitchBendRangeSemitones is unused: the ABI has no pitch wheel."
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "Tatami/Source/Devices/Instruments/EmberDevice.h",
        "sha256": "f5a8d957b8b69f27ce73380962818b015e88b76a4ac57e60f1f54fd15116738f",
        "portedTo": "cpp/devices/ember/ember.h",
        "deviations": [
          "The meter outputs (level, voices, lfo1, lfo2, ampEnv, filterEnv) are removed; active_voices() remains as a test hook.",
          "State for the pitch wheel and the sustain pedal is removed (see EmberDevice.cpp)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "Tatami/Source/Devices/Instruments/EmberDevice.cpp",
        "sha256": "443f0a4272a92acb51d7eef14d07d620336ada1177550204268a289c79fde385",
        "portedTo": "cpp/devices/ember/ember.h",
        "deviations": [
          "Notes arrive as note_on(note id, frequency, gain) instead of MIDI. The pitch is the fractional MIDI note of the frequency (frequency clamped to 8..13000 Hz, pitch to 0..127), the velocity is the gain clamped to 0..1, and voices and the mono/legato held-note stack are keyed by note id instead of note number. A NaN frequency is ignored; a NaN gain plays at 0.7.",
          "Pitch wheel, sustain pedal (CC 64) and all-notes-off are dropped: the ABI carries no such messages.",
          "Tempo-synced LFO rates are dropped (no tempo in the ABI).",
          "juce::dsp::Oversampling (2x, polyphase IIR half-band) is replaced by the decimating half of kit::Halfband2x, a 63-tap linear-phase FIR, one per channel. The engine renders at 2x directly, so there is no upsampling stage. Each pair of 2x samples is fed one 2x sample late, which makes the latency exactly 16 samples (latencySamples).",
          "Consequence of the FIR's transition band (flat to 0.42 fs, -80 dB from 0.58 fs): content between 24 and 27.8 kHz at the 2x rate is only partly removed and folds to 20.2..24 kHz. For a 1 kHz saw the worst such component is 45 dB under the fundamental, above 22 kHz. From 10 to 22 kHz aliasing measures 67 dB under the fundamental against 68 dB in the source.",
          "The output is clamped to +-1 after the decimator: the half-band can overshoot an already soft-clipped master by a fraction of a dB. The soft clip itself (linear to 0.5, knee to 1) is the source's and still runs at the 2x rate on the voice sum.",
          "kOutputTrim (0.36, -8.9 dB) scales the Volume gain. The source reaches -12 dBFS with one note at the default volume and puts chords into the clipper; with the trim one default note at gain 0.7 peaks at -23 dBFS and ten notes stay under the clip knee. Every preset is 8.9 dB quieter than in Tatami at the same Volume value.",
          "Each voice starts its oscillators at a different phase (golden-ratio steps per voice index, added to the source's per-unison-voice offsets). In the source all voices start in phase, so identical notes add coherently.",
          "The 32-sample control sub-blocks run on a counter across host blocks instead of restarting at every host block and MIDI event, so the output does not depend on the block size. Parameters that are not smoothed per sample advance their 5 ms ramp 32 samples at a time at the start of each sub-block.",
